Starting from Andreas Dorn's excellent Extended Conducts v2.3 patch,
which you can find via the bilious patch DB, I have, for reasons
that are not entirely clear even to me, created a patch that adds
support for a "stoner" roleplay conduct, which requires you to
remain under the effects of hallucination for the whole game.  With
this patch, if the player puts OPTIONS=stoned in .nethackrc, new
games will start with the character hallucinating and carrying a
supply of hallucinogens that *should*, if my calculations are
correct, be sufficient to sustain continuous hallucination for
thirty to forty thousand turns (though I have not tested this
duration in actual practice), longer if the player finds a way to
curse them, and of course they can be supplemented with potions of
hallucination (the player starts with one of those too, so it's
identified) and hallucinogenic corpses. I've tested that taking the
hallucinogens does cause hallucination, that a stoppage of
hallucination does violate the conduct, and that at the end of the
game a message is printed to the effect that you either "were
stoned the whole time" or "sold out to The Man and sobered up",
as the case may be.

If you do NOT have the option set in .nethackrc when you start
a game, your game should be unaffected as compared to normal
vanilla play.  (Technically, a spoiled player could wish for
the hallucinogen by name, but if you're not playing the conduct
there is no compelling reason to do so.  Finding it in bones
is also a theoretical possibility, if someone else on the
system is playing with the conduct.  So, if you're playing
on a system with this patch installed and do not want to
hallucinate, don't eat any bright green pills you find in
bones piles, especially if you don't have a unicorn horn.)

I would be interested in any feedback on this patch, and especially
on the hallucination conduct.  (The other conduct enhancements
from Andreas' patch are still included as well.  I just added the
hallucination parts and reworded a couple of messages.)

Does there need to be a warning message some number of turns
before your drugged state times out?  Are the 50 guaranteed
doses you start the game with enough?  Is the hallucination itself
the hardest part of keeping this conduct, or are the things you
have to avoid doing (e.g., using unicorn horns) in order to keep
from sobering up actually the harder part?  Can anyone actually
ascend with this conduct in tact?  Can it be combined with some
of the others for super multi-conduct runs?  What's the worst
other conduct to combine it with, in terms of difficulty?

Download, patch, compile, play, and let me know what you think.

Currently, the patch is for NetHack 3.4.3 and will apply either to
vanilla or to the NAO codebase.  At some point I would like to
update it for NH4, but I have not done so yet.

